//? Title: YOLO v5-style CSP features and mosaic fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Detecting digits of different sizes requires finding boxes and classes across several feature scales. This report checks CIoU, ratio/neighbour targets, CSP/SPPF/PAN graphs and byte-exact mosaic geometry, then visibly fits the compact detector with tensor Adam and paired BN checkpoints.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/yolo_v5_style.cpp`.

> The method

CSP branches, serial spatial pooling and a bidirectional PAN neck produce three prediction scales. Ratio/axial-neighbour assignment and detached-IoU objectness targets train the complete compact graph on explicit fixed-centre mosaics.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/yolo_v5_style_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/yolo_v5_style_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/yolo_v5_style_concept.tikz > build/yolo_v5_style_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/yolo_v5_style_concept.svg build/yolo_v5_style_concept.dvi > build/yolo_v5_style_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
