// result_end
\caption(Visible whole-model Adam on fit-only mosaics/flips and dynamic resolutions. Class BCE is shown with its.5 aggregate weight; the other trace contains CIoU and objectness. Validation selects paired learned/BN checkpoints.)
\alttext(Visible whole-model Adam on fit-only mosaics/flips and dynamic resolutions. Class BCE is shown with its.5 aggregate weight; the other trace contains CIoU and objectness. Validation selects paired learned/BN checkpoints.)

The selected epoch20 checkpoint has validation AP50.127463. On23 digits in
eight test scenes, AP50 is.063752, AP75.002704 and COCO AP50:95.017808,
with718 detections. Loss decreases, but the many false and misplaced boxes
show that this bounded compact fit generalizes poorly. These are demonstration
results on synthetic digit scenes, not a YOLO benchmark.

\image(figures/yolo_v5_style_detections.png)
\caption(Actual held-out predictions in red and truth boxes in green after paired checkpoint restoration. Errors and extra boxes remain in the reported evaluation.)
\alttext(Eight test scenes with predicted and true digit boxes.)

> Conclusion

The report separates initialized full-graph checks from compact whole-model fitting. Actual pixels, fit-only priors/augmentation, explicit optimization, paired BN restoration and held-out detections make both behavior and remaining errors inspectable without a benchmark claim.

> References

- [Ultralytics YOLOv5 v6.0 model configuration](https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/blob/v6.0/models/yolov5s.yaml).
- [Ultralytics YOLOv5 v6.0 loss and target construction](https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/blob/v6.0/utils/loss.py).
- [Zheng et al.(2020), Distance-IoU Loss: Faster and Better Learning for Bounding Box Regression](https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.08287).
